# Go Standards – riskengine

## Error Handling
- Always wrap errors with context: `fmt.Errorf("operation %s: %w", name, err)`
- Define sentinel errors in `errors.go` of each package using `errors.New`
- Never ignore errors with `_` unless explicitly commented with reason

## Naming
- Interfaces: suffix `er` (e.g., `RuleEvaluator`, `FeatureFetcher`)
- Constructors: `New<Type>(...)` returning `(*Type, error)`
- Context always first parameter: `func Foo(ctx context.Context, ...)`
- Unexported fields in structs; expose via methods

## Concurrency
- Use `errgroup.WithContext` for parallel goroutines with timeout
- Always pass `context.Context`; respect cancellation in loops
- Use `sync.Pool` for frequently allocated objects (DecisionContext, FeatureMap)
- Protect shared state with `sync.RWMutex`; prefer atomic for counters

## Performance
- Pre-allocate slices/maps with known capacity: `make([]T, 0, n)`
- Reuse objects via `sync.Pool`; reset before returning to pool
- Avoid `interface{}` boxing in hot paths; use concrete types
- Profile before optimizing; benchmark critical paths with `testing.B`

## Testing
- Table-driven tests; subtests with `t.Run`
- Mock interfaces with `mockery` or hand-written fakes in `_test` files
- Benchmarks for rule evaluation and feature fetching hot paths
- Integration tests under `internal/<pkg>/testdata/`

## Logging & Observability
- Use `go.uber.org/zap` structured logger; never `fmt.Println` in production code
- Propagate `TraceID` via context; extract in middleware
- Export Prometheus metrics from each subsystem via `pkg/metrics`

## Module
- Module: `github.com/yourorg/riskengine`
- Min Go version: 1.22
- Prefer stdlib; add external deps only with justification in PR description
